From: PowOS
Subject: present: a fence callback fires once (Xwayland hang in miSyncTriggerFence)

24.1's miSyncTriggerFence re-walks a fence's triggers until none fires (a
trigger may delete others). Present's trigger counted as firing for as long as
its callback was set, and nothing cleared it: when xwl_present_re_execute
requeued the request for a later MSC (KGSL surfaceless: no flips, frame
callbacks held back) the walk fired it again, forever, inside ProcSyncDispatch.
Xwayland spun a core and stopped serving clients (Steam's web UI, Proton games).

Clear the callback before calling it: it is armed only while the fence is
untriggered (present_execute_wait), so it is meant to run once. The fence may
be freed by the callback, so nothing touches it afterwards.
---
 present/present_fence.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/present/present_fence.c b/present/present_fence.c
--- a/present/present_fence.c
+++ b/present/present_fence.c
@@ -52,9 +52,14 @@
 present_fence_sync_trigger_fired(SyncTrigger *trigger)
 {
     struct present_fence        *present_fence = container_of(trigger, struct present_fence, trigger);
+    void                        (*callback)(void *param) = present_fence->callback;
+    void                        *param = present_fence->param;
 
-    if (present_fence->callback)
-        (*present_fence->callback)(present_fence->param);
+    if (callback) {
+        present_fence->callback = NULL;
+        present_fence->param = NULL;
+        (*callback)(param);
+    }
 }
 
 static void
